  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Suman Mishra And Others vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 18 September, 2024 Author: Gurpal Singh Ahluwalia Bench: G. S. Ahluwalia Neutral Citation No. 2024:Mphc-Jbp:47225 2024:Mphc 1 W.P. No.26391/2024 In The High Court Of Madhya Pradesh At Jabalpur BEFORE HON'BLE SHRI JUSTICE G. S. AHLUWALIA ON THE 18th OF SEPTEMBER, 2024 WRIT PETITION No. 26391 of 2024 SUMAN MISHRA AND OTHERS Versus THE STATE OF MADHYA PRADESH AND OTHERS Appearance: Shri Pravesh Naveriya - Advocate for the petitioners. Shri hri Mohan Sausarkar - Government Advocate for the respondents/State.",
    "facts": "It is submitted by counsel for petitioners that petitioner No.1 is father-in-law, law, petitioner No.2 is mother-in-law law and petitioner No.3 is unmarried sister-in--law law of respondent No.3. The brother of respondent NEUTRAL CITATION NO. 2024:MPHC-JBP:47225 2024:MPHC No.3 had Suman Mishra And Others vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 18 September, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/101527927/ 1 filed an application under Section Section 97 of Cr.P.C. before SDM SDM, Chhatarpur for her production on the ground that she is being harassed by her husband and he is assaulting her to an an extent which has created a danger to her life and accordingly, it was prayed that search warrant may be issued so that the life of the complainant/respondent No.3 may be saved. Thereafter, respondent No.3 lodged an FIR on 22.08.2023 against the petitioners and her husband for offence under Sections 498-A, 498 A, 323, 294, 506, 34 of IPC and under Section 3/4 of Dowry Prohibition Act. For about one month, she was kept properly properly by the petitioners and her husband and thereafter fter petitioners and her husband started harassing her physically and mentally on the ground of bringing less dowry. They were constantly alleging that her mother, brother and sister have not given sufficient dowry and were constantly demanding an amount of Rs.5 Lakh and a four wheeler.",
    "arguments": "The subject matter of proceedings under Section 97 of Cr.P.C. was as to whether the respondent No.3 was in illegal detention detention or not and therefore, it was not expected that the respondent No.3 should have spoken elaborately with regard to the cruelty committed by her each and every in-law. law. The investigation is at the initial stage."
  },
