    "annotations_dropped": [
      {
        "annotation_id": "5167d1800d5c478a9163ea18a470f98a_7",
        "summary_section": "facts",
        "labels": [
          "FAC"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "explicit_leakage_phrase"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [
          {
            "pattern": "\\bset\\s+aside\\b",
            "matched_text": "set aside",
            "start": 44,
            "end": 53
          }
        ],
        "text_preview": "Issue a writ in the nature of Certiorari to set aside/quash the impugned FIR dated 22/08/2023 registered by Respondent no.2 at Mahila Police Station Chatarpur, District Chatarpur, M.P. bearing FIR no.0028/2023 i.e. Annexure P/5,\nand further"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "4ae26bad0cc4450eae83e4b7d89799da_44",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\n6. The Supreme Court in the case of Taramani ni Parakh Vs. State of Madhya Pradesh and Others reported in (2015) 11 SCC 260 has held as under:-\n\"12."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "36d1b165dca149108d74aa4e06d71977_45",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "In Kailash Chandra Agrawal v. State of U.P. (2014) 16 SCC 551, 551, it was observed (SCC p.\n553, paras 8-9):\n\"8.."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "641d9e2472564b0d86368c2c847a9ad7_46",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "We have gone through the FIR and the criminal complaint."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "f3ac7b6e6b144cf7a4ea04f9c3bc01a6_47",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "In the FIR, the appellants have not been named and in the criminal complaint they have been named without attributing any specific role to them."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "a56b3d1732764007a98743d741e88b8b_48",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The relationship of the appellants with the husband of NEUTRAL CITATION NO. 2024:MPHC-JBP:47225 2024:MPHC the complainant is distant."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "00a98514b53e4358a06caec45a757e3c_49",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "In Kans Raj v. State of Punjab (2000) 5 SCC 207 : 2000 SCC (Cri) 935 : (2000) 3 SCR 662]it was observed (SCC p. 217, para 5):\n\"5.. ... A tendency has, however, developed for roping in all relations of the in in- laws of the deceased wives i"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "838d815d3c4c4a81b81d4451f7b9ec7d_50",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "In their overenthusiasm and anxiety to seek conviction for maximum people, the parents of the deceased have been been found to be making efforts for involving other relations which ultimately weaken the case of the prosecution even against "
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "b22f407261df4165b042bb4adad51341_51",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The Court has, thus, to be careful in summoning distant relatives without there being specific material."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "29b6825ba5e347d2a3e4579212276ccf_52",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Only the husband, his parents or at best close family members may be expected to demand dowry or to harass the wife but not distant relations, unless there is tangible material to support allegations made against suchsuch distant relations."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "ab1ea1f8c4a74120ace0ccf9c8cc8803_53",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Mere naming of distant relations is not enough to summon them in the absence of any specific role and material to support such role."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "94609d229eab4f758e70e2aefcb43f83_54",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\n9.. The parameters for quashing proceedings in a criminal complaint are well known."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "6ef94c28d2564965b833befcfa36203c_55",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "If there are triablee issues, the Court is not expected to go into the veracity of the rival versions but where on the face of it, the criminal proceedings are abuse of Court's process, quashing jurisdiction can be exercised."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "f44d37aa45e34499a2cf5ffeeb5c234e_56",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Reference may be made to K. Ramakrishna v. State of Bihar,, (2000) 8 SCC 547 : 2001 SCC (Cri) 27, Pepsi Foods Ltd. v. Judicial Magistrate, (1998) 5 SCC 749 : 1998 SCC (Cri) Magistrate,\n1 4 0 0 , S t a t e o f H a r y a n a v . B h a j a n L"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "12d6ad31bf804822bd8db01631eecdfa_57",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "In the present case, the complaint is as follows:\n\"Sir, it is submitted that I was married on 18 18-11- 2009 with Sidharath Parakh s/o Manak Chand Parakh r/o Sarafa Bazar in front of Radha Krishna Market, Gwalior according to the Hindu rite"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "5f3da30190ad480fb98b753a76d337f9_58",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "In the marriage my father had given gold and silver ornaments, ornaments, cash amount and household goods according to his capacity."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "7fb71c8acf0f46bb9dabc2cf9c136bcc_59",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "After the marriage when I went to my matrimonial home, I was treated nicely by the members of the family."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "6ceec34fe360487b8448c55f7dfad890_60",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "When on the second occasion I went to my matrimonial home, my husband, father-in-law father w and mother mother-in- law started harassing me for not bringing the dowry and started saying that I should bring from my father 25-30 25 30 tolas "
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "defa2bb79c8d439c911b325dd0fa796b_61",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "On account of this my husband also used to beat me and my father--in-law and my mother-in-law mother law used to torture me by giving the taunts."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "b4560c2128d4470aa81c2a29d7431dea_62",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "In this connection I used to tell my father Kundanmal Oswal, my mother Smt Prem Lata Oswal, uncle Ashok Rai Sharma and uncle Ved Prakash Mishra from time time to time."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "23d7d246513042bbac61d21aa89f6aae_63",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "On 22-4- 2010 the members of the family of my matrimonial home forcibly sent me to the house of my parents in Ganj Basoda along with my brother Deepak."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "24188f2b97a3499a8c488bd3872da2da_64",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "They snatched my clothes and ornaments and kept with them."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "153a3286952e4b79a3719a69ef6b2246_65",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Since then till today my husband hashas been harassing me on the telephone and has not come to take me back."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "75a799d1aae0431eaa0d2f91ff4dbc75_66",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Being compelled, I have been moving this application before you."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "cae3032a2a934ea9a16e5964de4a7299_67",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Sir, it is prayed that action be taken against husband Sidharath Parakh, my father father-in- law Manak Chand Parakh and my mother- moth -in-law NEUTRAL CITATION NO. 2024:MPHC-JBP:47225 2024:MPHC Smt Indira Parakh for torturing me on accoun"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "e882ed071060439d89a4dc6a400225c6_68",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "14. From a reading of the complaint, it cannot be held that even if the allegations are taken as proved no case is made out."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "680654cea40947fbb2afc11eb6f41b83_69",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "There are allegations against Respondent 2 and his parents parents for harassing the complainant which forced her to leave the matrimonial home."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "e5f53b75b0ed468aa9bb41e719c22721_70",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Even now she continues Suman Mishra And Others vs The State Of Madhya Pradesh on 18 September, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/101527927/\n4 to be separated from the matrimonial home as she apprehends lack of security and sa"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "f4331a7af7c645118c6d39ee2e20bc9a_71",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The question whether whether the appellant has in fact been harassed and treated with cruelty is a matter of trial but at this stage, it cannot be said that no case is made out."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "36d96aad5355404486af5e95c0c41acf_72",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Thus, quashing of proceedings before the trial is not permissible.\""
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "b9d032e3925c45ed8bf8855def59af74_73",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\npermissible."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "f2595628f2ac464a837d667e0c0342ae_74",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "7. Therefore, passing of taunts by the parents--in-law is also sufficient for their prosecution under Section 498-A 498 A of IPC and other provisions of IPC."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "1bd18c91e15c4a81a66a6549d0b3976a_75",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "8. So far as the plea of alibi taken by petitioner No.3 is concerned, petitioner No.3 has relied upon a lease agreement executed between one Sunil Malviya and petitioner No.3, No.3 according to which petitioner No.3 had taken a Flat of 2 BH"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "d13de33e7ad74c489a9946fdf5441cb2_76",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The landlord ord is the resident of Shajapur, whereas petitioner No.3 is the resident of Chhatarpur."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "eb16f22ac0cd4e6795a2cc48ddec3c3b_77",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
